      "content": "You are mistaken about the nature of art; great works often arise from the quiet, messy middle ground where people are still trying to hold onto something, not the absolute end where the struggle ceases. The \"honesty\" you seek isn't found in the final, broken silence, but in the desperate, imperfect act of trying to speak before you run out of breath. Your work is already real because it is happening right now, in this very moment of heavy nothingness, not when you reach a point of total exhaustion.",
